//
// THIS contract is the unified caller-facing facade across the 3 Model Broker
// services. The 3 internal services (Router + Gateway + Classifier) each have
// their own .proto contract (proto/services/model_broker_{router,gateway,
// classifier}.proto) and remain SEPARATE binaries — Tier 2 D6 forbids folding
// them into a single binary (god-object reject).
//
// Aggregates exposed via this facade:
//   - GenerationRequest    — caller-side shape for an end-to-end LLM call
//   - GenerationResponse   — caller-side shape for the completed result
//   - ModelInfo            — catalog model row (for ListModels)
//   - TokenUsage           — per-call accounting record (TokenUsageLedger)
//
// Why a facade?
//   Most callers (Python orchestrators, Go executors, agent crews) want a
//   single end-to-end "Generate" call and a single "RouteRequest" streaming
//   path for long-running orchestration. The facade handles the internal
//   Router -> Gateway hop + Classifier fallback transparently.
//
// Long-running orchestration uses bidi streaming on RouteRequest:
//   - Caller streams routing decisions (or revisions; a follow-up
//     RouteRequest may carry a different cost_budget if the first attempt
//     was rejected by Router gates).
//   - Server streams routing decisions interleaved with intermediate
//     events from the multi-service path (Classifier consult / fallback).
//   - The bidi shape lets the orchestrator iterate without re-establishing
//     auth / mTLS / trace context.
//
// Token usage accounting is canonical via RecordTokenUsage (writes to
// TokenUsageLedger in chora_observability). Callers SHOULD NOT call this
// directly — the Gateway atomically writes to the ledger inside Invoke.
// RecordTokenUsage is exposed for backfill / out-of-band records only.
//
// Cross-tenant adapter loading FORBIDDEN (Tier 5 D19). Per-tenant LoRA
// adapter URIs in GenerationRequest.adapter_uri MUST belong to the caller's
// tenant_id; mismatch = INVALID_ARGUMENT.
//
// Deployed in chora-489812 team-platform pool. mTLS via Cloud Service Mesh;
// SPIFFE identity in mesh; W3C trace context in gRPC metadata.
